# A missing hashed asset must be a REAL 404 — never the SPA fallback. Serving
# index.html (200, text/html) under an /assets/*.js URL is what poisoned
# browsers/edge during deploy races (the _headers immutable rule keys on the
# URL, so the HTML got cached for a year under the chunk's address — Jul 27/28
# incidents). The target page lives at the ROOT as assets-404.html — a root
# 404.html file flips Pages out of automatic SPA mode and 404s every deep-route
# refresh (Jul 28 regression: /timeclock reloads showed the 404 page).
/assets/* /assets-404.html 404

# SPA fallback: every other path serves the app shell; the client router takes
# over. (Pages also does this automatically while no root 404.html exists —
# keep it that way.)
/* /index.html 200
